  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A block of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"280\"></span> grams is attached to a horizontal spring of spring constant <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"43\"></span> N m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. The spring is then extended by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"38\"></span> cm. At <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span> the block is released and it oscillates with simple harmonic motion (SHM) between point A and point C. The period of the oscillations is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span>. Friction between the surface and the block is negligible.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. Draw a free-body diagram to represent the forces that act on the block at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = \\frac{3T}{8}\"></span>.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>b. On the diagram, label the position where the speed of the block is maximum.</p>\n<p>  [1]</p>\n<p>c. Calculate the maximum speed reached by the block.</p>\n<p>    [2]</p>\n<p>The graph shows how the displacement of the block from B varies with time. </p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure>\n\n<p>d. Sketch a graph to show how the acceleration of the block varies with time. </p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_04\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 4\" src=\"asset:fig_04\"/></figure>\n\n<p>  [2]</p>"
  },
